1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
Welcome to Topic 8.

2
00:00:01,850 --> 00:00:03,850
3, File Shares and Permissions.

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:10,100
A file server is only useful when the
right people can reach the right files,

4
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:11,950
and nobody else can.

5
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:17,400
In this topic you will meet SMB, the
protocol behind Windows file shares.

6
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:22,450
You will share a folder three ways:
Advanced Sharing, Server Manager and

7
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:23,900
PowerShell.

8
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:29,350
You will set share permissions and NTFS
permissions, and work out what happens

9
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:31,200
when the two combine.

10
00:00:31,450 --> 00:00:37,050
Then you will check access with Effective
Access and icacls, and compare SRV01 with

11
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:39,300
the NAS in your pod.

12
00:00:39,550 --> 00:00:41,950
SMB stands for Server Message Block.

13
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:47,400
When you type backslash backslash SRV01
backslash Projects, that is a UNC path,

14
00:00:47,650 --> 00:00:49,650
and SMB carries the conversation.

15
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:51,100
SMB 1.

16
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:53,350
0 is old and unsafe.

17
00:00:53,600 --> 00:01:00,000
Windows Server 2019 and later and Windows
11 do not install it, and you should never

18
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:01,450
add it back.

19
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:07,300
SMB 2 replaced it from 2007, and SMB 3 is
what you use today.

20
00:01:07,550 --> 00:01:11,950
Signing proves who sent each message and
that nobody changed it.

21
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:17,800
Windows 11 24H2 requires it both ways, and
Windows Server 2025 requires it for

22
00:01:18,050 --> 00:01:19,250
connections it opens.

23
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:22,300
Encryption is optional and off by default.

24
00:01:22,550 --> 00:01:27,350
A share has its own short permission list
with only three levels.

25
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:31,600
Read lets people see names, open files and
run programs.

26
00:01:31,850 --> 00:01:34,250
Change adds create, edit and delete.

27
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:38,100
Full Control adds changing NTFS
permissions and taking ownership.

28
00:01:38,350 --> 00:01:43,150
Remember one thing: share permissions are
checked only when someone comes through

29
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,400
the share over the network.

30
00:01:45,650 --> 00:01:49,650
Someone signed in at the server itself
never meets them.

31
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:52,300
So the common practice is simple.

32
00:01:52,550 --> 00:01:58,150
Give Authenticated Users Change, or Full
Control, at the share, and do the real

33
00:01:58,400 --> 00:01:59,600
control in NTFS.

34
00:01:59,850 --> 00:02:04,250
Advanced Sharing starts with Everyone
Read, so you swap that entry.

35
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:06,500
Here is the classic way.

36
00:02:06,750 --> 00:02:11,550
In File Explorer, open the folder's
Properties, the Sharing tab, and Advanced

37
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:13,000
Sharing.

38
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:14,850
Tick Share this folder.

39
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:18,700
The share name defaults to the folder
name, Projects.

40
00:02:18,950 --> 00:02:20,150
Then select Permissions.

41
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:24,000
In Permissions for Projects you see
Everyone with Read.

42
00:02:24,250 --> 00:02:28,650
Remove it, select Add, type Authenticated
Users and check the name.

43
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:30,500
Then tick Allow Change.

44
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:33,150
Read is ticked along with it.

45
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,400
Leave every Deny box clear.

46
00:02:35,650 --> 00:02:38,850
Select OK twice, and the folder is shared.

47
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:41,500
Nothing about NTFS has changed yet.

48
00:02:41,750 --> 00:02:42,950
That comes next.

49
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:45,600
Server Manager has a wizard too.

50
00:02:45,850 --> 00:02:50,250
In File and Storage Services, open Shares,
then Tasks, New Share.

51
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:52,500
First you pick a profile.

52
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:58,750
SMB Share Quick works for any folder and
is the one you would use here.

53
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:04,200
SMB Share Advanced adds quotas and needs
File Server Resource Manager, which is

54
00:03:04,450 --> 00:03:05,650
Topic 8.

55
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:07,100
4.

56
00:03:07,350 --> 00:03:11,750
The Other Settings page holds a key
option: Enable access-based enumeration,

57
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,200
or ABE.

58
00:03:13,450 --> 00:03:18,250
With ABE, users see only the files and
folders they can access.

59
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:20,900
dpatel will not even see Faculty-Only.

60
00:03:21,150 --> 00:03:23,150
But ABE only hides things.

61
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:25,800
NTFS still decides who gets in.

62
00:03:26,050 --> 00:03:29,250
In PowerShell, New-SmbShare does it in one
command.

63
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:33,900
Give the name and path, then ChangeAccess
for Authenticated Users, and

64
00:03:34,150 --> 00:03:36,550
FolderEnumerationMode AccessBased to turn
on ABE.

65
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:42,000
Because you name the access yourself,
there is no Everyone entry to remove.

66
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:45,850
Get-SmbShareAccess lists the share
permissions, one row per entry.

67
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:51,300
To change a right, revoke the entry with
Revoke-SmbShareAccess, then add it again

68
00:03:51,550 --> 00:03:55,550
with Grant-SmbShareAccess and the new
right: Full, Change or Read.

69
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:58,600
The Force switch skips the confirmation
question.

70
00:03:58,850 --> 00:04:04,450
NTFS permissions live on the files and
folders themselves, so they work over the

71
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:05,900
network and locally.

72
00:04:06,150 --> 00:04:10,950
The basic permissions are Full control,
Modify, Read and execute, List folder

73
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:12,800
contents, Read and Write.

74
00:04:13,050 --> 00:04:18,250
Modify is the everyday permission for
people who edit files; it includes delete

75
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:20,100
but not changing permissions.

76
00:04:20,350 --> 00:04:25,550
Each basic permission is really a bundle
of advanced permissions, such as Create

77
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:27,800
files, Delete or Change permissions.

78
00:04:28,050 --> 00:04:34,450
And permissions add up: a user gets every
Allow entry for the user and every group

79
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:36,300
the user is in.

80
00:04:36,550 --> 00:04:37,750
Permissions flow down.

81
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:43,600
A new folder inherits entries from its
parent, and C colon backslash gives the

82
00:04:43,850 --> 00:04:45,850
Users group Read and execute.

83
00:04:46,100 --> 00:04:50,900
So on Projects you disable inheritance and
set explicit entries: GG-Faculty Modify

84
00:04:51,150 --> 00:04:53,150
and GG-Students Read and execute.

85
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:55,800
Faculty-Only does the same, without
students.

86
00:04:56,050 --> 00:05:00,850
When entries disagree, explicit Deny wins
first, then explicit Allow, then inherited

87
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:02,700
Deny, then inherited Allow.

88
00:05:02,950 --> 00:05:04,150
Use Deny rarely.

89
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:07,200
It hits every member of a group.

90
00:05:07,450 --> 00:05:09,450
Removing an entry is cleaner.

91
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:12,100
This is where you do it.

92
00:05:12,350 --> 00:05:15,950
Open the folder's Properties, the Security
tab, and Advanced.

93
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:20,600
The list shows Type, Principal, Access,
Inherited from and Applies to.

94
00:05:20,850 --> 00:05:25,650
Every entry here comes from C colon
backslash, including two for Users.

95
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:27,100
Select Disable inheritance.

96
00:05:27,350 --> 00:05:30,950
Windows asks what to do with the inherited
entries.

97
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:35,200
Choose Convert: they stay as explicit
copies, so nothing breaks.

98
00:05:35,450 --> 00:05:39,850
The other choice removes them all and
leaves an empty list.

99
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:44,500
After converting, remove the Users entries
and add the GG groups.

100
00:05:44,750 --> 00:05:47,950
Now the most important rule in this topic.

101
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:53,000
A user on CLIENT01 who opens backslash
backslash SRV01 backslash Projects passes

102
00:05:53,250 --> 00:05:54,450
two gates.

103
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:57,100
First the share permissions, then NTFS.

104
00:05:57,350 --> 00:06:02,150
Work out each gate on its own, then take
the lower result.

105
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:08,800
cdiaz has Change at the share and Modify
in NTFS, so she can create, edit and

106
00:06:09,050 --> 00:06:10,250
delete.

107
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:17,300
dpatel has Change at the share but only
Read and execute in NTFS, so he can only

108
00:06:17,550 --> 00:06:18,750
read.

109
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:23,800
If you set the share to Read, cdiaz can
only read too.

110
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:27,250
At the server's own console, only NTFS
counts.

111
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:29,900
Remember AGDLP from Learning Plan 4.

112
00:06:30,150 --> 00:06:35,350
Accounts go into global groups, global
groups go into domain local groups, and

113
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:38,400
the domain local group gets the
permission.

114
00:06:38,650 --> 00:06:43,450
DL-Shared-Read is an example: it holds
GG-Faculty and GG-Students, and it got

115
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:47,300
Read on C colon backslash Shared in Lab 6.

116
00:06:47,550 --> 00:06:48,750
2.

117
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,200
In Lab 8.

118
00:06:50,450 --> 00:06:56,050
3 you take a shortcut and give the GG
groups the NTFS entries directly.

119
00:06:56,300 --> 00:06:59,100
In one small domain that is fine.

120
00:06:59,350 --> 00:07:03,750
The full AGDLP way would use groups such
as DL-Projects-Modify and

121
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:07,600
DL-Projects-Read, so a new group needs
only a membership.

122
00:07:07,850 --> 00:07:11,450
How do you know what someone can really
do?

123
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:15,300
Use the Effective Access tab in Advanced
Security Settings.

124
00:07:15,550 --> 00:07:19,950
Choose Select a user, type cdiaz, and
select View effective access.

125
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:24,600
Windows adds up every entry for her and
all her groups.

126
00:07:24,850 --> 00:07:28,850
Each permission gets a green check or a
red X.

127
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:34,700
For cdiaz on Projects you see read, write
and delete allowed, but Full control,

128
00:07:34,950 --> 00:07:37,350
Change permissions and Take ownership
denied.

129
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:43,200
The Access limited by column tells you
which gate said no: file permissions or

130
00:07:43,450 --> 00:07:44,650
the share.

131
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:46,900
The tab never changes anything.

132
00:07:47,150 --> 00:07:49,950
icacls shows the same list as text.

133
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:54,200
OI and CI mean files and subfolders
inherit the entry.

134
00:07:54,450 --> 00:07:59,250
M is Modify, RX is Read and execute, F is
Full control.

135
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:01,900
CREATOR OWNER has IO, inherit only.

136
00:08:02,150 --> 00:08:05,350
It is a template, not a real user.

137
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:11,600
When cdiaz creates Plan dot txt over the
share, she becomes the owner, and Windows

138
00:08:11,850 --> 00:08:17,450
turns that template into an entry for her:
Full control, marked I for inherited.

139
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:23,300
So she can change permissions on her own
file, while other faculty only have

140
00:08:23,550 --> 00:08:24,750
Modify.

141
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,600
Get-Acl shows the owner.

142
00:08:26,850 --> 00:08:31,650
Run Get-SmbShare on any server and you see
shares you never made.

143
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:37,900
C dollar for each drive, ADMIN dollar for
the Windows folder, and IPC dollar for

144
00:08:38,150 --> 00:08:39,350
remote management.

145
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:41,200
Windows creates them itself.

146
00:08:41,450 --> 00:08:47,450
The dollar sign hides a share from browse
lists, and only administrators can use C

147
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:49,300
dollar and ADMIN dollar.

148
00:08:49,550 --> 00:08:53,150
Leave them in place; remote tools depend
on them.

149
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:56,200
Offline files is the other idea here.

150
00:08:56,450 --> 00:09:02,450
The share's caching setting lets a laptop
keep working when the server is out of

151
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:04,300
reach, then sync later.

152
00:09:04,550 --> 00:09:07,350
The default lets users pick the files.

153
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:11,600
Your pod has a second file server, NAS01,
running TrueNAS.

154
00:09:11,850 --> 00:09:15,850
A NAS is an appliance managed from a web
page.

155
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:21,300
It also speaks SMB, so users see a share
just like on SRV01.

156
00:09:21,550 --> 00:09:23,150
The difference is identity.

157
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:29,000
NAS01 is not in the domain, so it uses its
own local account, nasuser.

158
00:09:29,250 --> 00:09:33,250
SRV01 uses Active Directory groups, NTFS,
ABE and Effective Access.

159
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:39,100
To connect, type net use, the drive
letter, the path, slash user colon NAS01

160
00:09:39,350 --> 00:09:41,350
backslash nasuser, and a star.

161
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:46,800
Name NAS01 in front, because otherwise
Windows sends your domain, SA1, and the

162
00:09:47,050 --> 00:09:49,850
NAS only knows its own local account.

163
00:09:50,100 --> 00:09:55,700
The star makes Windows ask for the
password, so it never appears on the

164
00:09:55,950 --> 00:09:57,150
command line.

165
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:59,000
Four mistakes to avoid.

166
00:09:59,250 --> 00:10:04,450
One: locking down the share but leaving
Users Read and execute in NTFS.

167
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:08,300
Every domain user can still read through
the share.

168
00:10:08,550 --> 00:10:10,550
Disable inheritance and remove Users.

169
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:13,600
Two: adding Deny for students on
Faculty-Only.

170
00:10:13,850 --> 00:10:15,450
Just remove their entry.

171
00:10:15,700 --> 00:10:19,300
Three: choosing Remove all inherited
permissions instead of Convert.

172
00:10:19,550 --> 00:10:23,150
The folder ends up with no entries at all.

173
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:25,400
Four: testing only as Administrator.

174
00:10:25,650 --> 00:10:27,650
Administrators can open almost anything.

175
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:33,500
Sign in as cdiaz and dpatel, and check the
Effective Access tab for each.

176
00:10:33,750 --> 00:10:34,950
Check yourself.

177
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:38,800
Projects has the share permission
Authenticated Users Change, NTFS

178
00:10:39,050 --> 00:10:43,450
GG-Faculty Modify and GG-Students Read and
execute, and ABE is on.

179
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:46,500
First: the share is changed to Read.

180
00:10:46,750 --> 00:10:51,150
What can cdiaz do over the network, and at
SRV01 itself?

181
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,800
Second: dpatel does not see Faculty-Only.

182
00:10:54,050 --> 00:10:58,050
Why, and what happens if he types the full
path?

183
00:10:58,300 --> 00:11:02,700
Third: why does cdiaz have Full control on
Plan dot txt?

184
00:11:02,950 --> 00:11:08,550
Fourth: can dpatel save a new file in
Projects, and which gate stops him?

185
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,000
Pause and answer.

186
00:11:10,250 --> 00:11:11,850
Here are the answers.

187
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:16,900
One: read only over the network, because
the most restrictive gate wins.

188
00:11:17,150 --> 00:11:21,150
At SRV01 there is no share, so she keeps
Modify.

189
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:28,200
Two: dpatel has no entry on Faculty-Only,
so ABE hides it, and if he types the path,

190
00:11:28,450 --> 00:11:30,050
NTFS gives access denied.

191
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:36,300
Three: she created the file, so she owns
it, and the CREATOR OWNER entry became

192
00:11:36,550 --> 00:11:38,150
Full control for her.

193
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:39,600
Four: no.

194
00:11:39,850 --> 00:11:44,650
The share allows Change, but NTFS gives
GG-Students only Read and execute.

195
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:47,300
Let's do it in the pod.

196
00:11:47,550 --> 00:11:53,150
On SRV01 I create the Projects folder, and
icacls shows the Users entries it

197
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:54,600
inherited.

198
00:11:54,850 --> 00:11:59,650
I share it with Advanced Sharing, remove
Everyone and give Authenticated Users

199
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:01,100
Change.

200
00:12:01,350 --> 00:12:04,550
In Server Manager I turn on access-based
enumeration.

201
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:09,600
In Advanced Security Settings I disable
inheritance, convert, remove Users and add

202
00:12:09,850 --> 00:12:11,450
the two GG groups.

203
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:14,500
Faculty-Only gets its own list without
students.

204
00:12:14,750 --> 00:12:17,550
Effective Access confirms dpatel has
nothing there.

205
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:20,200
On CLIENT01, cdiaz creates a file.

206
00:12:20,450 --> 00:12:23,250
dpatel cannot see Faculty-Only and cannot
write.

207
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:24,700
To wrap up.

208
00:12:24,950 --> 00:12:28,550
Use SMB 3 with signing, and keep SMB 1.

209
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:30,000
0 off.

210
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:34,250
Share permissions have three levels: Full
Control, Change and Read.

211
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:38,100
NTFS permissions use inheritance, explicit
entries and, rarely, Deny.

212
00:12:38,350 --> 00:12:41,550
Over the network the most restrictive gate
wins.

213
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:45,400
Check the result with Effective Access,
ABE and icacls.

214
00:12:45,650 --> 00:12:46,850
In Lab 8.

215
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:52,300
3, about 75 minutes and practice only, you
share and secure Projects, build

216
00:12:52,550 --> 00:12:57,750
Faculty-Only, test as cdiaz and dpatel,
and map the NAS share from CLIENT01.
